        "detail": "All verified. Here is the full deployment report:\n\n---\n\n## Deployment Report: trusty-console\n\n### Version\n`trusty-console 0.1.0` (from `crates/trusty-console/Cargo.toml`)\n\n### Worktree\n`/Users/masa/Projects/trusty-tools/.claude/worktrees/deploy-console` — left in place as instructed.\n\n### Build\nBuilt from the worktree with `cargo build --release -p trusty-console`. The UI `dist/` directory was already committed (pre-built vanilla-JS placeholder), so the `build.rs` pnpm step was not needed. Build completed clean in ~13 seconds.\n\n### Install\n`cargo install --path crates/trusty-console --locked --force` from the worktree root. The `--force` flag was required because `trusty-console` was already on PATH as a bundled binary produced by the previous `trusty-search` install. The atomic `cargo install` replace-rename path ensures the macOS kernel cdhash cache stays consistent.\n\n### Running: launchd agent\nConfigured at `~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.trusty.console.plist`, consistent with the existing `com.trusty.search`, `com.trusty.memory`, and `com.trusty.mpm` pattern:\n- **Label:** `com.trusty.console`\n- **Command:** `~/.cargo/bin/trusty-console serve --http 127.0.0.1:7788`\n- **KeepAlive:** yes (restarts on non-zero exit)\n- **RunAtLoad:** yes\n- **Logs:** `~/Library/Logs/trusty-console/stdout.log` and `stderr.log`\n- **PID at verification time:** 86695 (`state = running`)\n\n### Endpoint Verification (raw output)\n\n```\ncurl -s http://127.0.0.1:7788/api/console/services\n```\n\n```json\n[{\"id\":\"trusty-search\",\"display_name\":\"Trusty Search\",\"status\":\"running\",\"version\":\"0.24.4\",\"url\":\"http://127.0.0.1:7878\"},{\"id\":\"trusty-memory\",\"display_name\":\"Trusty Memory\",\"status\":\"running\",\"version\":\"0.15.2\",\"url\":\"http://127.0.0.1:7070\"},{\"id\":\"trusty-analyze\",\"display_name\":\"Trusty Analyze\",\"status\":\"running\",\"version\":\"0.7.0\",\"url\":\"http://127.0.0.1:7879\"}]\n```\n\nThree services detected and reported as running.\n\n### Startup log (stderr)\n```\nINFO poller: starting background health-poll (interval=15s)\nINFO trusty-console listening on http://127.0.0.1:7788\ntrusty-console: http://127.0.0.1:7788\n```\n\nNo errors.\n\n### FDA / Codesign Note\nFull Disk Access re-grant is **not required** for trusty-console. It only reads `~/.local/share/trusty-*` discovery files and makes localhost HTTP requests — it does not access `/Volumes/` external mounts or other TCC-gated paths. The codesign cdhash issue is handled by using `cargo install` (which atomically renames to `~/.cargo/bin/trusty-console`), keeping the kernel's signing cache consistent.\n\n### Additional Note\nA pre-existing `trusty-console serve --http 0.0.0.0:7788` process (PID 79806) was present from a prior manual run, but it is not under launchd supervision. The launchd-managed instance on `127.0.0.1:7788` (PID 86695) is the one serving and will survive reboots. If you want to kill the unmanaged stray: `kill 79806`.",
