        "detail": "Both done. Here's the summary.\n\n## 1. Open issues — core services (29 of 117 open issues)\n\n**trusty-search (20)** — dominated by a fresh cluster of **5 critical warm-boot/index data-integrity bugs filed 2026-06-11** (#1091, #1090, #1089, #1088, #1087): silent 0-chunk loads, resurrection of pruned indexes, config-file clobbering, wrong-index removal. Plus three scaling epics (#704/#705/#706) and the #607 line-cap refactor sweep (30 files).\n\n**trusty-memory (3)** — **#1096** (split the 5,421-line `web.rs`, just filed), #463 (fd/LRU redb handle cap), #340 (deferred BM25 opts, cross-listed with search).\n\n**trusty-analyze (1)** — #972 (generic SARIF ingest, shared with search #819).\n\n**trusty-common (3 + cross-crate)** — #989/#985 cleanup (prune migration flags, extract `daemon_guard`), #833 (shared events/tool-registry/intent harness); plus #692 backing-store eval and the #814–#819 KG-extensibility set that spans search/analyze/common.\n\n**Top candidates to act on next:**\n1. **#1091–#1088** — critical trusty-search data-integrity bugs (block safe reindex). Highest priority.\n2. **#1096** — trusty-memory `web.rs` 11× over cap, blocks growth/testing.\n3. **#993** — lazy warm-boot (sequence *after* the bug cluster).\n4. **#819 + #814** — KG extensibility ADR/API, blocks #817/#818.\n5. **#607** — line-cap refactor sweep (steady-state).\n\n## 2. Console deployed ✅\n\n- **trusty-console 0.1.0** built from an isolated worktree, installed atomically via `cargo install` (no `cp` — cdhash-safe).\n- Running under **launchd** (`com.trusty.console`, KeepAlive+RunAtLoad, `127.0.0.1:7788`, PID 86695), consistent with the other `com.trusty.*` agents. Logs in `~/Library/Logs/trusty-console/`.\n- **Verified live** — `GET /api/console/services` returns all three core daemons as `running`: trusty-search 0.24.4 (:7878), trusty-memory 0.15.2 (:7070), trusty-analyze 0.7.0 (:7879). No FDA/codesign re-grant needed (localhost + PATH only).\n\n⚠️ **One cleanup item:** a pre-existing **unmanaged** `trusty-console` process (PID 79806, bound `0.0.0.0:7788`) from a prior manual run is still around. Since it shares port 7788 with the launchd instance, it's a conflict/ambiguity risk. Want me to have local-ops kill the stray (`kill 79806`) so only the supervised launchd instance serves?\n\nNote: this was a review + local deploy only — no issues were modified and nothing was committed/pushed. Want me to spin up the top-priority trusty-search bug cluster (#1087–#1091) next?",
