        "title": "Perfect. Now let me format these as a structured digest:",
        "tags": [],
        "detail": "Perfect. Now let me format these as a structured digest:\n\n---\n\n## Issue Digests: #1087–#1091 (trusty-search Data Integrity Bugs)\n\n### #1087 — trusty-search index remove -i ignores index flag, removes CWD-detected index instead\n\n**Reported behavior / repro:**\n- From inside repo A's directory, run `trusty-search index remove -i someOtherIndex`\n- Observes: repo A's index (CWD-detected) is removed, not `someOtherIndex`\n- Caused accidental removal of `trusty-tools` and `APEX` indexes twice in one session\n\n**Expected behavior:**\n- `-i`/`--index` flag should override auto-detected project index when given\n- Per documentation: \"override the auto-detected project index\"\n- When `-i` is provided, **never** fall back to CWD detection\n\n**Root-cause hints / affected code:**\n- CLI flag parsing: `-i` / `--index` flag not being honored as removal target\n- Likely in the `index remove` subcommand handler (trusty-search CLI)\n\n**Labels:**\n- `bug`, `trusty-search`\n\n---\n\n### #1088 — Flipping index colocated flag silently wipes central store data\n\n**Reported behavior / repro:**\n- Index registered with `colocated=true` but data actually lives in central store\n- Set `colocated=false` in `indexes.toml` to match actual location\n- Restart daemon\n- Observes: central store dir is reset/emptied\n\n**Expected behavior:**\n- On colocated-mode change, either migrate existing data to new location OR refuse with clear error\n- **Never silently wipe data**\n\n**Root-cause hints / affected code:**\n- Data loss: 436MB (cto), 213MB (duetto-backend), 120MB (duetto-frontend) of HNSW data\n- Affected files: `indexes.toml`, central store initialization logic on daemon startup\n- Component: colocated mode transition / data directory initialization\n\n**Labels:**\n- `bug`, `trusty-search`\n\n---\n\n### #1089 — PATCH /indexes/<id> rewrites indexes.toml from daemon state, stripping manual edits\n\n**Reported behavior / repro:**\n1. Hand-edit `indexes.toml` to add/change `exclude_globs` or other manual settings\n2. Issue any `PATCH` request on a **different index** (e.g., to change root_path)\n3. Observes: `indexes.toml` is rewritten from in-memory state, losing the manual edits\n\n**Expected behavior:**\n- `PATCH` should perform targeted field update only, not full rewrite of on-disk config\n- Use merge-update pattern instead of replacement\n\n**Root-cause hints / affected code:**\n- HTTP handler: `PATCH /indexes/<id>` endpoint\n- File I/O: Full serialization of daemon state to `indexes.toml` instead of selective merge\n- Impact: `exclude_globs` edits overwritten, `colocated` flags reset to true for multiple indexes\n\n**Labels:**\n- `bug`, `trusty-search`\n\n---\n\n### #1090 — Warm-boot resurrects pruned indexes from leftover central-store data dirs\n\n**Reported behavior / repro:**\n1. `trusty-search index remove <id>` (drops registration from `indexes.toml`, leaves data dir on disk)\n2. Daemon restart\n3. Observes: index reappears with full data\n\n**Expected behavior:**\n- Either: CLI `index remove` should optionally delete the data dir (like HTTP DELETE does)\n- OR: Warm-boot should **only** load indexes present in `indexes.toml`, not auto-register orphan data dirs\n- Avoid implicit resurrection of pruned indexes\n\n**Root-cause hints / affected code:**\n- Warm-boot scan: auto-discovery of orphaned data directories under `~/Library/Application Support/trusty-search/indexes/*`\n- Central store data dir scanning logic\n- Impact: pruned down to 7 active indexes via CLI, but warm-boot re-registered ~100 stale indexes\n\n**Labels:**\n- `bug`, `trusty-search`\n\n---\n\n### #1091 — Warm-boot colocated scan timeout (default 10s) silently loads 0 chunks on large roots\n\n**Reported behavior / repro:**\n1. Index with large colocated root (e.g., 126GB mount containing Google-Drive-style data)\n2. Daemon restart\n3. Observes: `trusty-search status` or health check shows index loaded but with 0 chunks\n4. Timeout failure not visibly surfaced; no obvious error signal\n\n**Expected behavior:**\n- Either: Surface clear health/log signal when index is skipped due to scan timeout (distinct from \"healthy empty index\")\n- OR: Skip known-mount/excluded paths during warm-boot scan itself so excludes apply pre-timeout and reduce scan time\n\n**Root-cause hints / affected code:**\n- Warm-boot scan timeout: default 10 seconds via `TRUSTY_WARMBOOT_INDEX_TIMEOUT_SECS` env var\n- Colocated index loading logic\n- Impact: `cto` index (126GB root on slow mount) timed out and served 0 chunks\n- Failure mode: opaque—not clearly distinguished from healthy empty index\n\n**Labels:**\n- `bug`, `trusty-search`\n\n---\n\n## Summary\n\nAll 5 issues are **trusty-search data-integrity and state-management bugs** affecting:\n\n1. **CLI flag handling** (#1087) — `-i` flag not overriding CWD detection\n2. **Colocated mode transitions** (#1088) — silent data wipes on flag flip\n3. **Config file merging** (#1089) — PATCH rewrites instead of merge-updates `indexes.toml`\n4. **Warm-boot auto-discovery** (#1090) — resurrects pruned indexes from orphaned dirs\n5. **Timeout opacity** (#1091) — 0-chunk silent load on colocated scan timeout\n\nKey files/concepts mentioned:\n- `indexes.toml` (configuration state file)\n- Central store data directories: `~/Library/Application Support/trusty-search/indexes/*`\n- Colocated flag: boolean controlling where HNSW data is stored\n- Warm-boot scan: daemon startup index discovery\n- HTTP `PATCH /indexes/<id>` handler\n- CLI `index remove` subcommand\n- Environment variable: `TRUSTY_WARMBOOT_INDEX_TIMEOUT_SECS`",
