        "detail": "trusty-review verdict: **APPROVE\\*** (approve with advisories) — no blocking issues, good traceability and regression tests. But two things must be tightened before merge, because these are silent-data-loss bugs and the margin for \"advisory\" is thin here:\n\n1. **Medium / real risk:** the #1088 fix falls back to `unwrap_or(true)` when the on-disk entry can't be read — a transient read error would re-assume `colocated=true` and re-trigger the exact wipe it's meant to prevent. Should fall back to the in-memory `colocated` value.\n2. **My standing concern on #1089:** both the engineer's and reviewer's framing describe the fix as *colocated-flag preservation only*. #1089's actual complaint is broader — a PATCH on one index rewrites the whole `indexes.toml` and strips manual edits like `exclude_globs` on **other** indexes. That broader case may still be unfixed.\n\nPlus the #1087 unit test doesn't actually exercise the explicit-id branch it's named for, so that fix lacks real automated coverage. I'm sending it back to the same engineer/worktree to close these before merge.",
