        "time": "23:04",
        "who": "rust-engineer",
        "title": "Pushed. Now the Manual QA Checklist for all 5 bugs:",
        "tags": [],
        "detail": "Pushed. Now the Manual QA Checklist for all 5 bugs:\n\n---\n\n## Manual QA Checklist — PR #1097 (5 bugs)\n\nUse an **isolated temp daemon** — not the live daemon on :7878. Every step below assumes you launched a fresh test daemon pointing at a temp data directory:\n\n```bash\n# terminal A — isolated daemon\nTRUSTY_DATA_DIR=$(mktemp -d) TRUSTY_NO_KG=1 RUST_LOG=warn \\\n  cargo run -p trusty-search -- start --port 17878\nexport TS_PORT=17878\nBASE=http://127.0.0.1:$TS_PORT\n```\n\n---\n\n### Bug #1088 / Issue 1 — colocated fallback is `false` (safe value)\n\n**Setup**: register a central-store (non-colocated) index.\n```bash\nTMP_A=$(mktemp -d)\ncurl -s -X POST $BASE/indexes \\\n  -H 'content-type: application/json' \\\n  -d \"{\\\"id\\\":\\\"qa-central\\\",\\\"root_path\\\":\\\"$TMP_A\\\"}\" | jq .\n# expect: {\"id\":\"qa-central\",\"created\":true}\n```\n\n**Test**: simulate a missing disk entry by removing the index from `indexes.toml` (if accessible) or simply confirm the fallback path via the existing unit test output.\n```bash\ncargo test -p trusty-search -- colocated_fallback_is_false_when_disk_entry_absent --nocapture\n```\n**Pass criteria**: test prints `ok`; no panic; fallback resolves to `colocated = false`.\n\n**Manual smoke**: do a PATCH relocate to a new path and confirm the index stays in the central data dir (not moved inside `$TMP_A`).\n```bash\nTMP_B=$(mktemp -d)\ncurl -s -X PATCH $BASE/indexes/qa-central \\\n  -H 'content-type: application/json' \\\n  -d \"{\\\"root_path\\\":\\\"$TMP_B\\\"}\" | jq .\n# expect: {\"id\":\"qa-central\",\"relocated\":true,...}\n# verify data dir still under $TRUSTY_DATA_DIR (not under TMP_B)\nls $TRUSTY_DATA_DIR/indexes/\n```\n**Pass criteria**: `ls` shows `qa-central/` (or similar) still in the central store; `TMP_B` does not contain an index sub-directory.\n\n---\n\n### Bug #1089 / Issue 2 — PATCH index A does not strip exclude_globs from index B\n\n**Setup**: register two indexes, hand-edit `indexes.toml` to add `exclude_globs` to B.\n```bash\nTMP_A=$(mktemp -d); TMP_B=$(mktemp -d)\ncurl -s -X POST $BASE/indexes \\\n  -H 'content-type: application/json' \\\n  -d \"{\\\"id\\\":\\\"qa-a\\\",\\\"root_path\\\":\\\"$TMP_A\\\"}\" | jq .\ncurl -s -X POST $BASE/indexes \\\n  -H 'content-type: application/json' \\\n  -d \"{\\\"id\\\":\\\"qa-b\\\",\\\"root_path\\\":\\\"$TMP_B\\\"}\" | jq .\n```\n\nFind and edit `indexes.toml` (in `$TRUSTY_DATA_DIR`), adding `exclude_globs = [\"*.log\"]` to the `qa-b` entry. Restart the daemon to pick up the edit, then:\n```bash\n# PATCH index A only\ncurl -s -X PATCH $BASE/indexes/qa-a \\\n  -H 'content-type: application/json' \\\n  -d \"{\\\"root_path\\\":\\\"$TMP_A\\\"}\" | jq .\n```\n\n**Verify**: `grep exclude_globs $TRUSTY_DATA_DIR/indexes.toml` — the `*.log` entry must still be present under `qa-b`.\n\n**Pass criteria**: `qa-b`'s `exclude_globs` survives the PATCH to `qa-a`. Also run the unit regression test:\n```bash\ncargo test -p trusty-search -- patch_index_a_does_not_strip_exclude_globs_of_index_b --nocapture\n```\n\n---\n\n### Bug #1090 / Issue 3 — atomic DELETE (root_path capture + unregister under one lock)\n\nThe atomicity guarantee is validated by the unit test; the manual check confirms no leftover roots.toml entry.\n\n```bash\nTMP_C=$(mktemp -d)\ncurl -s -X POST $BASE/indexes \\\n  -H 'content-type: application/json' \\\n  -d \"{\\\"id\\\":\\\"qa-delete\\\",\\\"root_path\\\":\\\"$TMP_C\\\"}\" | jq .\ncurl -s -X DELETE $BASE/indexes/qa-delete | jq .\n# expect: {\"id\":\"qa-delete\",\"removed\":true}\n```\n\n**Verify**: the warm-boot roots file no longer contains `$TMP_C`:\n```bash\ngrep \"$TMP_C\" $TRUSTY_DATA_DIR/roots.toml && echo \"FAIL: root still present\" || echo \"PASS: root removed\"\n```\n\n**Unit test** (covers the TOCTOU scenario directly):\n```bash\ncargo test -p trusty-search -- registry_remove_and_get_returns_handle_atomically --nocapture\ncargo test -p trusty-search -- registry_remove_and_get_returns_none_for_missing_id --nocapture\n```\n\n**Pass criteria**: both unit tests pass; `roots.toml` does not contain the deleted path.\n\n---\n\n### Bug #1087 / Issue 4 — `-i <id>` bypasses CWD detection\n\n**Setup**:\n```bash\nTMP_X=$(mktemp -d); TMP_Y=$(mktemp -d)\ncurl -s -X POST $BASE/indexes \\\n  -H 'content-type: application/json' \\\n  -d \"{\\\"id\\\":\\\"qa-x\\\",\\\"root_path\\\":\\\"$TMP_X\\\"}\" | jq .\ncurl -s -X POST $BASE/indexes \\\n  -H 'content-type: application/json' \\\n  -d \"{\\\"id\\\":\\\"qa-y\\\",\\\"root_path\\\":\\\"$TMP_Y\\\"}\" | jq .\n```\n\n**Test** from within `$TMP_X` (so CWD auto-detection would pick `qa-x`), but pass `-i qa-y`:\n```bash\n# Run index remove dry-run equivalent: use --daemon-url flag to point at test port\ncd $TMP_X\n# The binary reads $TS_PORT via daemon_base_url → set TRUSTY_SEARCH_PORT:\nTRUSTY_SEARCH_PORT=$TS_PORT cargo run -p trusty-search -- index remove -i qa-y\n# expect: \"Removed index \"qa-y\" …\"\n# qa-x must still exist:\ncurl -s $BASE/indexes/qa-x/status | jq .index_id\n# expect: \"qa-x\"\n```\n\n**Unit test**:\n```bash\ncargo test -p trusty-search -- index_remove_explicit_id_bypasses_path_lookup --nocapture\n```\n\n**Pass criteria**: unit test passes; manual invocation removes `qa-y`, not `qa-x`.\n\n---\n\n### Bug #1073 / Issue 5 — warm-boot integrity (original 5-bug suite)\n\nThese are the three bugs from #1073 plus the two relocation bugs. Covered by the existing `tests_1073` suite:\n\n```bash\ncargo test -p trusty-search -- tests_1073 --nocapture\n```\n\n**Expected output** (all pass, ~5 tests):\n- `relocate_index_returns_404_for_unknown_id` — ok\n- `relocate_index_updates_root_path` — ok\n- `hash_cache_relative_key_matches_after_load` — ok\n- `colocated_fallback_is_false_when_disk_entry_absent` — ok\n- `patch_index_a_does_not_strip_exclude_globs_of_index_b` — ok\n\n**Daemon-level smoke** (warm-boot round-trip):\n```bash\nTMP_W=$(mktemp -d)\ncurl -s -X POST $BASE/indexes \\\n  -H 'content-type: application/json' \\\n  -d \"{\\\"id\\\":\\\"qa-warmboot\\\",\\\"root_path\\\":\\\"$TMP_W\\\"}\" | jq .\n# stop + restart daemon, then:\ncurl -s $BASE/indexes/qa-warmboot/status | jq .\n# expect: root_path = TMP_W (not a default fallback path), chunk_count ≥ 0\n```\n\n**Pass criteria**: all unit tests pass; after restart the index status returns the correct `root_path`.\n\n---\n\nAll five checks complete. Tear down the test daemon:\n```bash\ncurl -s -X POST $BASE/shutdown || kill $(lsof -ti :$TS_PORT)\n```",
