        "detail": "Now I have the evidence I needed:\n\n- **#1089 resolved & explained:** persistence uses read-all → overwrite-only-the-target → save-all (`upsert_index_registry_entry_at`), so other indexes' on-disk fields (incl. manual `exclude_globs`) are loaded and re-saved verbatim — never stripped. Backed by a passing regression test.\n- **#1088 fallback** is now `unwrap_or(false)` (safe central-store direction; a read error can never flip an index to colocated/wipe).\n- **#1090 atomicity** fixed via `remove_and_get` using `DashMap::remove` (single shard lock across lookup+removal).\n- **`tests_1073`** is a pre-existing module (issue #1073 relocate handler) reused as the natural home for the relocate tests — not mislabeled; #1087/#1090 tests live in their own modules.\n- **Raw verification:** 1,066 tests pass / 0 fail, clippy clean, fmt clean, line-cap OK. Branch pushed; CI head matches.\n\nThese are silent-data-loss bugs, so unit tests alone don't satisfy my verification gate — I want real runtime evidence on a **throwaway** daemon (never the live :7878 with your ~100 real indexes). Running live QA against an isolated temp daemon and watching CI to completion in parallel.",
