        "detail": "Memory write is blocked (the trusty-memory HTTP daemon holds the palace write lock, so the stdio MCP can't write) — not worth a detour; the work is durably captured in the merged squash commit, closed issues, and commit messages. \n\nHere's where things landed.\n\n## ✅ Phase 1 complete — critical trusty-search bug cluster shipped\n\n**PR #1097 squash-merged to `main`** as `ba0d5c56`, closing **#1087, #1088, #1089, #1090, #1091**.\n\n| Bug | Root cause | Fix |\n|---|---|---|\n| #1087 | `main.rs` dropped `cli.index`, only passed the path | `-i <id>` now overrides CWD detection; never falls back |\n| #1088 | relocate hardcoded `colocated:true` | Loads on-disk value; fallback is `unwrap_or(false)` — a read error can never flip to colocated/wipe |\n| #1089 | PATCH stripped other indexes' manual edits | Persistence reads-all/overwrites-one/saves-all → sibling `exclude_globs` survive |\n| #1090 | delete left root in `roots.toml` | New atomic `remove_and_get` (DashMap shard lock) removes the root → no warm-boot resurrection |\n| #1091 | `degraded` flag ignored timeouts | `/health` now exposes `indexes_skipped_timeout` + flips `warm_boot_degraded` on timeout |\n\n**Verification (full ownership, not self-reported):**\n- 1,066 unit tests pass; clippy/fmt/line-cap clean; **all 6 CI checks green**.\n- **trusty-review: APPROVE\\*** — its two medium advisories were remediated before merge.\n- **Runtime QA on an isolated throwaway daemon** (`:17878`, temp data dir) — all 5 PASS with observed evidence (data file survived the PATCH, untouched index's `exclude_globs` survived, deleted index did not resurrect after restart). The live `:7878` daemon was **never contacted** (confirmed still up with its real indexes).\n\nWorktrees and feature branches cleaned up.\n\n## ⚠️ One action for you\nYour **live trusty-search is still 0.24.4** — the fixes are on `main` but not deployed. To pick them up: `cargo install --path crates/trusty-search --locked` + graceful restart. Mind the two known gotchas on restart: **#873** (re-grant Full Disk Access after `cargo install`) and **#874** (shutdown-hang at high index counts). I'd suggest running the isolated-daemon QA checklist once more against the freshly-built binary before restarting the real daemon. Want me to have local-ops handle that redeploy (carefully, with the FDA/restart steps)?\n\n## Deferred top candidates (not started — per your \"critical bugs first\" choice)\n- **#1096** — split the 5,421-line trusty-memory `web.rs`\n- **#993** — selective/lazy warm-boot\n- **#814 + #819** — KG extensibility ADR + API\n- **#607** — line-cap refactor sweep (30 files)\n\nWant me to pick up **#1096** next (concrete/mechanical, good follow-on), or queue several of the deferred items?",
