        "detail": "Pushed. Here is the full report:\n\n---\n\n**Fix applied**\n\nFile changed: `crates/trusty-memory/src/web/tests/attribution_tests.rs`\n\nTwo lines removed — one in each affected test:\n- `drawer_creator_attribution_http_default` (line 93, pre-fix)\n- `drawer_creator_attribution_http_header` (line 176, pre-fix)\n\nIn both cases `std::mem::forget(tmp)` was removed. The `tmp: TempDir` binding now lives to end of scope, so its `Drop` impl deletes the directory when the test function returns. No assertions were changed; only the lifetime management was fixed.\n\n**Was this pre-existing?**\n\nYes — carried over verbatim from the original monolithic `web.rs`. The split commit (`86a6490d`) that PR #1099 introduces performed a mechanical extraction of the test code; it did not add the `mem::forget` calls. They were already present at the same call sites in `web.rs` going back at least to the `9c9f3d62` fix commit. The trusty-review flag is therefore on the split, not on new code.\n\nNote: `test_state()` in `mod.rs` still uses `mem::forget` intentionally — that helper is designed to produce a globally-shared, leak-the-temp-dir state for tests that share setup overhead. The two attribution tests were replicating the pattern unnecessarily in their own bodies; they should (and now do) hold the handle locally.\n\n**Raw verification output**\n\n`cargo test -p trusty-memory 2>&1 | tail -20`:\n```\ntest result: ok. 1 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in 0.16s\n\n     Running tests/serve_stdio_e2e.rs (...)\n\nrunning 4 tests\ntest stdio_serve_recall_all_bounded ... ok\ntest stdio_serve_remember_and_recall_bounded ... ok\ntest stdio_serve_tools_list_bounded ... ok\ntest stdio_serve_stdout_is_only_json ... ok\n\ntest result: ok. 4 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in 1.45s\n\n   Doc-tests trusty_memory\n\nrunning 0 tests\n\ntest result: ok. 0 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in 0.00s\n```\n\n`cargo clippy -p trusty-memory --all-targets -- -D warnings 2>&1 | tail -5`:\n```\n   Compiling trusty-memory v0.15.2 (...)\n    Finished `dev` profile [unoptimized + debuginfo] target(s) in 5.22s\n```\n(zero warnings — clippy exited 0)\n\n`cargo fmt --check && echo FMT_CLEAN`:\n```\nFMT_CLEAN\n```\n\n`bash scripts/check_line_cap.sh 2>&1 | tail -3`:\n```\nline-cap: 166 allowlisted, 0 violations — OK.\n```\n\n**Push confirmed**: `86a6490d..a5c57dfb refactor/memory-web-split -> refactor/memory-web-split`",
