        "title": "Crystal clear now — and that settles my question, so no need to ask further:",
        "tags": [],
        "detail": "Crystal clear now — and that settles my question, so no need to ask further:\n\n> **Services = data only.** Each service just answers API requests for metrics. **The console is the sole renderer** — it pulls those metrics and turns them into native HTML in a tabbed SPA. No iframes, no service-emitted HTML.\n\nThat's the **Option A** architecture (console → service HTTP metrics APIs → console renders), and it's the right one. Stray console process is **killed** (only the launchd-managed instance serves :7788 now).\n\nHere's the concrete build I'll execute:\n\n- **trusty-console SPA** (Svelte, served from the daemon): a tab bar — **Overview** + one tab per detected service (**Search / Memory / Analyze**).\n- **Console daemon** gains metrics-aggregation routes (e.g. `GET /api/console/metrics/<service>`) that call each running service's existing HTTP metrics/health/stats API via `reqwest` and return normalized JSON.\n- **Each tab** renders that JSON as native HTML — e.g. Search: index list, chunk/RSS counts, embedder info, warm-boot/lazy state; Memory: palaces & drawer counts; Analyze: recent analyses/metrics. Overview keeps the running/available/absent cards.\n- Rebuild → reinstall → restart the launchd console → **Web-QA the actual rendered tabs** in a browser.\n\nI have a scoping pass already in flight mapping the current console UI/build setup and exactly which metrics each service's API exposes (so the renderer targets real fields, not guesses). The moment that lands I'll dispatch the implementation — I won't ask anything further unless a service genuinely exposes no usable metrics endpoint.\n\nIn parallel, #993's PR #1103 CI is being watched so it's ready to merge; the #607/#815 campaign stays paused while we land this console work. I'll report when the scoping returns and the build is underway.",
