        "detail": "trusty-review came back **REQUEST_CHANGES** on #1103 (not a rubber-stamp — good). It flagged four *confirmed* medium issues, two of which are genuine bugs:\n\n1. **Relocate handler drops LRU timestamps** — sets `last_queried_unix`/`last_indexed_unix` to `None` despite a comment claiming it preserves them, so a relocated index loses warm-boot priority. (Same class of \"relocate drops fields\" bug we just fixed in #1097 — needs the same read-existing-then-copy treatment.)\n2. **TOCTOU race** in the lazy loader → spurious 404 when an index finishes loading concurrently.\n3. **Sync disk read on every search hot-path** (`read_last_queried_unix` parses `indexes.toml` per query) — a real perf regression at scale; should be an in-memory cache.\n4. **Global `POST /search` silently excludes cold indexes** — with a warm-boot cap, fan-out returns partial results with no signal. Needs at minimum a `cold_indexes_skipped` count.\n\nI will **not** merge until these are fixed. Sending it back to the engineer.",
