        "detail": "Commit created and branch pushed. Here is the full report.\n\n---\n\n## PR #1103 Review Findings — Fix Report\n\n**Branch**: `feat/lazy-warm-boot`\n**New head SHA**: `9d09ca31`\n\n---\n\n### Finding 1 — BUG: Relocate drops LRU timestamps\n\n**File**: `crates/trusty-search/src/service/server/indexes_relocate.rs`\n\n**Change**: Replaced the two separate `load_index_registry()` calls (one for `colocated`, one implicit) with a single disk load that extracts all three preserved fields:\n\n```rust\nlet on_disk = crate::service::persistence::load_index_registry()\n    .ok()\n    .and_then(|entries| entries.into_iter().find(|e| e.id == id));\nlet on_disk_colocated = on_disk.as_ref().map(|e| e.colocated).unwrap_or(false);\nlet on_disk_last_queried = on_disk.as_ref().and_then(|e| e.last_queried_unix);\nlet on_disk_last_indexed = on_disk.as_ref().and_then(|e| e.last_indexed_unix);\n\n// ... PersistedIndex construction:\nlast_queried_unix: on_disk_last_queried,\nlast_indexed_unix: on_disk_last_indexed,\n```\n\n**Test** (`tests_1073.rs` — `relocate_preserves_lru_timestamps`): writes a `PersistedIndex` with `last_queried_unix: Some(1_700_000_000)` / `last_indexed_unix: Some(1_699_000_000)` to a temp TOML, applies the extraction pattern directly, and asserts both values round-trip. A second case with `None` timestamps confirms they are preserved as `None`.\n\n---\n\n### Finding 2 — BUG: TOCTOU race in `get_or_load_index`\n\n**File**: `crates/trusty-search/src/service/lazy_loader/loader.rs`\n\n**Change**: When `loading_gate` returns `None` (concurrent `mark_loaded` removed the cold entry), re-check the hot registry before returning `NotFound`:\n\n```rust\nlet gate = match cold_store.loading_gate(id) {\n    Some(g) => g,\n    None => {\n        // The cold entry vanished: a concurrent load raced us and won.\n        return registry.get(id).ok_or(LazyLoadError::NotFound);\n    }\n};\n```\n\n**Test** (`lazy_loader/mod.rs` — `get_or_load_index_gate_none_but_index_just_became_hot`): the injected `restore_fn` calls `registry.register(handle)` and `cold_store.mark_loaded(&id)` to simulate a concurrent load before `loading_gate` returns `None`, then asserts the result is `Ok`.\n\n---\n\n### Finding 3 — PERF: Sync disk read on hot query path\n\n**Files**: `server/state.rs`, `server/state_impl.rs`, `server/search.rs`\n\n**Change**: Added `last_queried_write_cache: Arc<DashMap<IndexId, u64>>` to `SearchAppState`. The hot path in `search_handler` now reads the in-memory map instead of opening `indexes.toml`:\n\n```rust\nlet stale = state\n    .last_queried_write_cache\n    .get(&index_id)\n    .map(|prev| now_unix.saturating_sub(*prev) >= LAST_QUERIED_WRITE_INTERVAL_SECS)\n    .unwrap_or(true);\nif stale {\n    state.last_queried_write_cache.insert(index_id.clone(), now_unix);\n    tokio::spawn(async move {\n        if let Err(e) = persistence::update_last_queried_unix(&id_str, now_unix) {\n            tracing::debug!(\"last_queried_unix update failed for '{id_str}': {e}\");\n        }\n    });\n}\n```\n\nThe map is updated immediately (before `tokio::spawn`) so concurrent queries in the same interval don't all race to spawn writes.\n\n**Test** (`tests_search.rs` — `last_queried_cache_rate_limits_disk_writes`): calls `search_handler` twice in rapid succession, asserts `last_queried_write_cache` is populated after the first call and the cached timestamp is unchanged after the second (rate-limited).\n\n---\n\n### Finding 4 — SILENT CORRECTNESS: Global fan-out excludes cold indexes\n\n**Files**: `server/search_global.rs`, `lazy_loader/store.rs`\n\n**Change**: Added `ColdIndexStore::count_matching` to count cold entries by ID without exposing the internal `DashMap`. In `global_search_handler`, computed `cold_indexes_skipped` before the `registry.list()` fan-out and included it in both the empty-result and normal response:\n\n```rust\nlet cold_indexes_skipped: usize = if let Some(requested) = req.indexes.as_ref() {\n    state.cold_store.count_matching(requested.iter().map(|s| s.as_str()))\n} else {\n    state.cold_store.len()\n};\n// Both response paths include: \"cold_indexes_skipped\": cold_indexes_skipped\n```\n\nHandler doc comment notes: lazy-loading all cold indexes on fan-out is deliberately not done; a follow-up issue should track \"opt-in load-all on global search\" as a separate semantic decision.\n\n**Test** (`tests_search.rs` — `test_global_search_surfaces_cold_indexes_skipped`): registers one hot index in `registry` and one cold entry in `cold_store`, calls `global_search_handler`, parses the response JSON, and asserts `cold_indexes_skipped == 1`.\n\n---\n\n### TODO(#796) confirmation\n\nThe `seen_legacy_ids` rename in `start.rs` slightly widens `failed_count` under-reporting of cold legacy entries (they were counted as \"warm\" under the old name). This is a pre-existing, unambiguous TODO comment referencing issue #796 in the source. No regression was introduced by this PR. Not fixed here.\n\n---\n\n### Follow-up issue recommendation\n\nYes, file one: **\"opt-in load-all on global search (`POST /search`)\"**. The current fix surfaces `cold_indexes_skipped` so callers know fan-out is incomplete. The deeper question — whether a caller should be able to pass `load_cold: true` and have the handler lazily load all cold indexes before fanning out — is a separate semantic decision with non-trivial latency implications and deserves its own design discussion before implementation.\n\n---\n\n### Raw verification output (from before commit)\n\n```\ncargo test -p trusty-search (tail -25):\ntest result: ok. 214 passed; 0 failed; 6 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out\n\ncargo clippy -p trusty-search --all-targets -- -D warnings (tail -5):\n    Finished `dev` profile [unoptimized + debuginfo] target(s) in ...\n\ncargo fmt --check:\nFMT_CLEAN\n\nbash scripts/check_line_cap.sh (tail -3):\nline-cap: 166 allowlisted, 0 violations — OK.\n```\n\n**LOC delta**: +443 inserted, −39 deleted (net +404 — driven almost entirely by new tests; production code changes are minimal).",
