        "detail": "**Feasibility investigation launched** (background). It's covering: how trusty-search ingests content (and whether a non-code/synthetic corpus fits), the data sources (`git log --since`/`-n N`, `git for-each-ref`, `gh pr list`), reusing **tga**'s existing git parser instead of rebuilding it, the **KG synergy** (commits/PRs as nodes with \"Changes/Touches\" edges — ties into the #814–819 work in flight), three design options (separate \"changes\" index vs. code-chunk annotation vs. KG nodes), incremental freshness for a rolling N-day window, and a recommended MVP with effort/risk. I'll report the assessment when it returns.\n\nFor situational awareness, here's everything currently running in parallel:\n\n| Thread | State |\n|---|---|\n| Console 0a (PR #1107) — parameterizing MCP client identity per review | finishing |\n| KG #815 — canonical edge-kind convergence | building |\n| Git-history indexing — feasibility | investigating |\n\n**One thing awaiting your nod** (the contract sign-off I promised, no rush): the shared `console_metrics` contract that landed in 0a —\n```\nmethod:  \"console_metrics\"   (MCP tool any local service exposes, no args)\nreport:  { service_id, display_name, version,\n           status: ok|degraded|error,\n           metrics: <opaque per-service JSON>,\n           metrics_schema_version: u32,\n           collected_at_unix?: u64 }\n```\ntrusty-review praised it; it's clean and extensible. I'll wire trusty-analyze to it (Phase 0b) once you're good with this shape — flag any change and I'll fold it in before anything depends on it. Nothing else needed from you meanwhile; I'll report as each thread lands.",
