        "detail": "Noted — #1107's CI surfaced a failing test: `embedder_client::supervisor::tests::from_env_uses_defaults_when_no_vars_set` (expected `5`, got `99`). That's a **flaky env-var test race** — another test sets that value to `99` and this one, lacking `#[serial]`/env-cleanup, reads it under parallel execution. It passed locally (serial) but failed in CI's parallel run. It's a real test-isolation bug that must be fixed before #1107 can merge — and it's not the clientInfo change's fault, just exposed by the new test module reordering.\n\nI can't dispatch into the `console-foundation` worktree right now because the clientInfo-identity fix is actively running in it. So the sequence is: let that agent land (it'll push + re-trigger CI), then I'll fold in the env-isolation fix for the embedder supervisor tests (`#[serial]` + `remove_var`) in the same worktree so CI goes deterministically green. I'll handle it on completion — no action needed from you.\n\nQuick status of the parallel threads:\n\n| Thread | State |\n|---|---|\n| Console 0a (PR #1107) | clientInfo fix running → then I fix the flaky embedder test → re-review/merge |\n| KG #815 convergence | building |\n| Git-history indexing feasibility | investigating |\n\nI'll report when the next one lands.",
