        "detail": "The feasibility investigation is back — short version: **highly feasible, and smaller than expected.**\n\n## Git-history indexing — feasibility findings\n\n**Core question (can trusty-search index non-code content?) → Yes, no engine changes needed.** The indexer's `index_file(path, content)` / `add_chunk` paths take arbitrary `(path, content)` strings — content doesn't have to come from a real file walk. A synthetic path like `git/<sha>.md` routes through the Markdown chunker; `root_path` just has to be a real dir.\n\n**We already have the hard part.** `tga` (trusty-git-analytics) has a production-grade git extractor — commits, per-file diff stats, branch + timezone-correct date windowing (`GitCollector::since/until`), and a rate-limited GitHub **PR** client. It's a workspace crate, so reuse is a trivial path dep. No need to rebuild git parsing.\n\n**Recommended MVP (effort: Small):** a `trusty-search changes` subcommand that, given `--repo` + `--since N days`, materializes each commit (+ optional PRs) as a small Markdown doc (subject, author, date, message body, changed-file stats — **not** raw diffs, to avoid bloat) into a **separate `<project>-changes` index**, queryable standalone or via `search_all`. The smallest first slice is **BM25-only** (`lexical_only` + `skip_kg`) — no ONNX, rebuilds in seconds, so \"why did auth change?\" works almost immediately. Rolling N-day window = wipe-and-rebuild on a schedule/on-demand.\n\n**Notable synergy with what's building right now:** the richer Phase 2 — modeling commits/PRs as **KG nodes with `Touches`/`Changes` edges to the files they changed** (\"show me every commit that touched `fn authenticate`\") — depends on exactly the **edge-kind extensibility (#814–819)** we're mid-campaign on. So the KG work unlocks this. Phase-3 git-blame recency would belong in trusty-analyze.\n\n**Risks** are minor/managed: index bloat (embed stats not diffs), `gh` auth (make PR indexing opt-in; commits work offline via git2), tga dep (trivial).\n\nRecommendation: make it an **epic** (Phase 1 MVP corpus → Phase 2 KG edges after #814–819 → Phase 3 blame), referencing #122 (branch-aware search) and #814–819.\n\nWant me to **ticket this as an epic** now? I'd file it but keep it queued behind the in-flight console + KG work (which, conveniently, is the prerequisite for its best part). Meanwhile: the console 0a clientInfo fix and KG #815 are still building, and I'll fold in the flaky-embedder-test fix on #1107 as soon as its worktree frees up.",
