        "detail": "<task-notification>\n<task-id>a7946f8bdeb7e680f<\/task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01K4gjxgU6ACRyUDmgMR73yj<\/tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-masa-Projects-trusty-tools/077cc4c2-20bd-4d8a-9291-03ab8cdbdf33/tasks/a7946f8bdeb7e680f.output<\/output-file>\n<status>completed<\/status>\n<summary>Agent \"Parameterize MCP client identity (#1107)\" completed<\/summary>\n<result>Done. Here is the full report:\n\n---\n\n## Final Report\n\n### The Fix\n\nThe trusty-review MEDIUM flag was correct: the original `build_initialize_request` hardcoded `\"trusty-common\"` as `clientInfo.name` in the MCP `initialize` handshake. This was a library that gets used by multiple callers, each of which should advertise its own identity.\n\n**API (how callers pass identity):**\n```rust\n// Callers pass their identity as the third argument to spawn:\nStdioMcpClient::spawn(\"trusty-memory\", &amp;[\"serve\"], \"trusty-agents\").await?;\n\n// The name flows: spawn() → stored in client_name field → initialize() → build_initialize_request(id, &amp;self.client_name) → clientInfo.name\n```\n\nThe signature is `spawn(binary: &amp;str, args: &amp;[&amp;str], client_name: impl Into&lt;String&gt;) -&gt; Result&lt;Self&gt;`. There is no default — all callers must supply a name. This is the cleaner API choice: no misleading default, no ambiguity.\n\n### trusty-agents Identity Preserved\n\nAll three call sites pass `\"trusty-agents\"` exactly:\n- `crates/trusty-agents/src/plugins/trusty_memory.rs`\n- `crates/trusty-agents/src/plugins/trusty_search.rs`\n- `crates/trusty-agents/src/tools/mcp_service_tools.rs`\n\nZero behavior change for existing MCP servers that trusty-agents connects to.\n\n### Verification Output (raw)\n\n**`cargo build -p trusty-common --features stdio-mcp-client,console-metrics`**\n```\nFinished `dev` profile [unoptimized + debuginfo] target(s) in 0.49s\n```\n\n**`cargo test -p trusty-common --features stdio-mcp-client,console-metrics 2&gt;&amp;1 | tail -15`** (stdio_mcp tests specifically):\n```\ntest stdio_mcp_client::tests::extract_result_errors_when_missing_result ... ok\ntest stdio_mcp_client::tests::extract_result_maps_error_object ... ok\ntest stdio_mcp_client::tests::extract_result_returns_inner_result ... ok\ntest stdio_mcp_client::tests::initialize_envelope_is_well_formed ... ok\ntest stdio_mcp_client::tests::plugin_slug_extracts_stem ... ok\ntest stdio_mcp_client::tests::spawn_missing_binary_errors ... ok\ntest stdio_mcp_client::tests::ids_are_monotonic ... ok\ntest stdio_mcp_client::tests::read_line_skips_non_json_prefix_lines ... ok\ntest stdio_mcp_client::tests::is_alive_returns_false_after_child_exits ... ok\ntest stdio_mcp_client::tests::call_tool_errors_when_respawn_unavailable ... ok\n```\n\n**`cargo test -p trusty-agents 2&gt;&amp;1 | tail -10`**\n```\ntest project_inspect_returns_agent_match ... ok\ntest result: ok. 2 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in 0.09s\n```\n\n**`cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings 2&gt;&amp;1 | tail -5`**\n```\n    Finished `dev` profile [unoptimized + debuginfo] target(s) in 7.55s\n```\n(zero warnings after the main crates — the tga duplicate warning is pre-existing and unrelated)\n\n**`cargo fmt --check &amp;&amp; echo FMT_CLEAN`**\n```\nFMT_CLEAN\n```\n\n**`bash scripts/check_line_cap.sh 2&gt;&amp;1 | tail -3`**\n```\nline-cap: 166 allowlisted, 0 violations — OK.\n```\n\n### New HEAD SHA\n\n`400f912fa3c11a5016d17e54ac5b57ff1a0f685d`<\/result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>105975<\/subagent_tokens><tool_uses>77<\/tool_uses><duration_ms>499839<\/duration_ms><\/usage>\n<\/task-notification>",
