        "detail": "Done. Here is the complete report.\n\n---\n\n**Root cause**\n\nThe race involved `TRUSTY_EMBEDDERD_MAX_RESTARTS`. `parse_env_uses_override` sets it to `\"99\"` and cleans up afterward, but in a parallel test run its `set_var` can execute between `from_env_uses_defaults_when_no_vars_set`'s `remove_var` and its `SupervisorConfig::from_env()` call — so the defaults test sees `99` instead of the expected `5`. The save/restore guard already present in `from_env_uses_defaults_when_no_vars_set` is insufficient by itself because it does not serialize execution; it only ensures cleanup when that test runs alone.\n\n**Isolation fix applied**\n\n1. Added `serial_test = { workspace = true }` to `[dev-dependencies]` in `crates/trusty-common/Cargo.toml` (workspace already had `serial_test = \"3\"`).\n2. Added `use serial_test::serial;` import to `supervisor_tests.rs`.\n3. Added `#[serial]` to all three env-mutating tests:\n   - `from_env_uses_defaults_when_no_vars_set`\n   - `parse_env_uses_override`\n   - `locate_binary_respects_explicit_override`\n\nNo production code was changed.\n\n**Raw verification output**\n\n```\ntest embedder_client::supervisor::tests::locate_binary_respects_explicit_override ... ok\ntest embedder_client::supervisor::tests::from_env_uses_defaults_when_no_vars_set ... ok\ntest embedder_client::supervisor::tests::parse_env_uses_override ... ok\n\n35 passed; 0 failed   (full trusty-common suite with embedder features)\n\nclippy: Finished `dev` profile — zero warnings\nFMT_CLEAN\nline-cap: 166 allowlisted, 0 violations — OK.\nAll pre-commit hooks: Passed\n```\n\n**New head SHA**: `daf409d7`",
