        "tags": [],
        "detail": "**#1112 (Console 0b) is merging** in the background (verified E2E), and its minor advisories are captured as **#1115**.\n\n**#1114 review came back REQUEST_CHANGES** (D+) — correctly. Several real items:\n- **Custom label not validated** — `Custom(\"\")`→`\"custom:\"`, `Custom(\"custom:foo\")`→`\"custom:custom:foo\"` (introduced here; needs a checked constructor).\n- **`bfs_neighbors` hardcodes `CallsFunction`** — meaning `callers_of`/`callees_of` ignore all other edge kinds, and the round-trip test uses `callees_of`, so it could pass *even if the new `custom:` edges weren't actually surviving warm-boot*. That undercuts the proof of #816 — must verify the custom-edge survival test observes those edges directly.\n- **`fact_hash_str` uses `DefaultHasher`** (not stable across Rust versions) for *persisted* entity IDs — a real durability flag; need to know if it's new here or pre-existing before touching it.\n- Plus trivial nits (panic→`unreachable!`, no-op coverage test, duplicate log).\n\nSending #1114 back for remediation before merge.",
