        "time": "11:15",
        "who": "rust-engineer",
        "title": "All done. Here is the full report:",
        "tags": [],
        "detail": "All done. Here is the full report:\n\n---\n\n## Remediation Report — PR #1114 (feat/kg-custom-hybrid)\n\n### 1. Custom Label Validation (Finding #1 — issue #818)\n\n**What was added:**\n\n- `EdgeKindError` enum (`EmptyLabel` | `LabelContainsColon(String)`) with `thiserror::Error` derive, defined in `contracts/edge_kind.rs`\n- `EdgeKind::custom(label: impl Into<String>) -> Result<Self, EdgeKindError>` — checked constructor that rejects:\n  - Empty strings → `EdgeKindError::EmptyLabel`\n  - Strings containing `':'` → `EdgeKindError::LabelContainsColon(s)` (prevents `Custom(\"custom:foo\")` → `\"custom:custom:foo\"` double-prefix)\n- `from_tag()` now validates the `custom:` suffix: returns `None` for empty suffix (`\"custom:\"`) and colon-containing suffix (`\"custom:foo:bar\"`), consistent with `custom()` invariants\n- `EdgeKindError` re-exported from `contracts::EdgeKindError` and `symgraph::EdgeKindError`\n- Doc comment on the `Custom(String)` variant now documents both invariants and the `from_tag` malformed-tag behavior\n- New tests: `edge_kind_custom_constructor_rejects_invalid`, `edge_kind_from_tag_rejects_malformed_custom`\n\n### 2. Warm-Boot Test Integrity (Finding #2 — issue #816)\n\n**Assessment of existing tests:** The existing `test_custom_edge_survives_warm_boot` was **already adequate** — it uses `loaded.all_edges()` (not `callees_of`) to observe the edge, so it would have caught Custom edges being dropped. `test_load_from_corpus_counts_unknown_edge_tags` already asserts both `edge_count() == 0` AND `unknown_edge_tags_dropped() == 1`.\n\n**What was added:** Doc notes on `callers_of` and `callees_of` in `traverse.rs` explicitly documenting that they traverse **only `CallsFunction` edges by design**, and directing callers to `neighbors_by_edge` or `all_edges` for non-call edge kinds.\n\n### 3. `fact_hash_str` Provenance (Finding #3)\n\n**Finding: PRE-EXISTING.** `git log --follow` shows `fact_hash_str` existed in `crates/trusty-common/src/symgraph/contracts.rs` on `origin/main` with identical `DefaultHasher` implementation (commits going back to `48dc38e7` and `6bd5438c`). This PR only moved the function into the split `contracts/mod.rs` during the contracts file split.\n\n**Action taken:** The `DefaultHasher` algorithm was NOT changed (changing it would invalidate already-persisted entity IDs — a migration concern for a separate ticket). The misleading doc comment was corrected: removed \"stable\" and \"cross-version\" language, added an explicit caveat that `DefaultHasher` is NOT guaranteed stable across Rust versions or process restarts.\n\n### 4. Trivial Nits (Finding #4)\n\n- `static_tag()` Custom arm: `panic!(...)` → `unreachable!(\"static_tag called on Custom — use tag() instead\")`\n- `edge_kind_union_coverage` test: replaced all `let _ = …` no-ops with a real `Vec<EdgeKind>`, asserts `len() == 30`, asserts each `tag()` is non-empty, and asserts each variant round-trips via `from_tag`\n- `load_from_corpus` duplicate warn: the format-string interpolated count `\"dropped {} edge(s) … {count}\"` was removed; only the structured field `dropped = g.unknown_edge_tags_dropped` is kept\n\n### 5. File Split (Line Cap)\n\n`edge_kind.rs` grew to 573 lines after the additions. The test module was extracted to `edge_kind_tests.rs` (204 lines) and wired via `#[cfg(test)] #[path = \"edge_kind_tests.rs\"] mod tests;`. Both files are under the 500-line cap. The pre-commit hook `check_line_cap.sh` confirms 0 violations.\n\n### Verification Output (Raw)\n\n```\ncargo build --workspace             → Finished dev profile — 0 errors\ncargo test -p trusty-common ...     → 75 passed; 0 failed (including all 8 edge_kind tests)\ncargo test -p trusty-search ...     → 6 passed; 0 failed (including custom warm-boot, tag round-trip)\ncargo test -p trusty-analyze ...    → 2 passed; 0 failed\ncargo clippy --workspace ...        → Finished — 0 new warnings (tga pre-existing 1 warning unrelated)\ncargo fmt --check                   → FMT_CLEAN\nbash scripts/check_line_cap.sh      → 165 allowlisted, 0 violations — OK\n```\n\n### New Head SHA\n\n`c2c4a56fe55e02528199a4e64a9184769ee5b5fc` pushed to `origin/feat/kg-custom-hybrid`",
        "calls": [],
        "outcome": "All done. Here is the full report:  ---  ## Remediation Report — PR #1114 (feat/kg-custom-hybrid)  ### 1. Custom Label Validation (Finding #1 — issue #818)  **What was added:**  - `EdgeKindError` enum",
