        "detail": "Noted — and that's a key architectural steer: the knowledge layer should be **developed jointly from trusty-memory (palace memories) AND the trusty-search KG (symgraph)**, not from memory alone. That actually closes the loop on what we just built — the canonical `EdgeKind` + `Custom(String)` edges + the #819 ingest overlay are precisely the KG substrate this would derive knowledge over.\n\nSo the epic will frame it as: palace memories + the symgraph KG → a derived canonical-knowledge layer (recurring/high-confidence facts promoted, related memories consolidated via KG relationships, conflicts/staleness handled) — deliberately lighter than the CTO fact-canonicalization model, which the research is mining now for exactly what to avoid.\n\nI've got this captured; I'll bake the dual **trusty-memory + trusty-search-KG** architecture into the epic when the research draft returns, and route it to ticketing then. The investigation is running in the background; nothing needed from you meanwhile. (In-flight in parallel: the **#1117** tga merge and the **#819** KG-ingest build — I'll report as each lands.)",
